    skos:definition "(4) If:  (a) a submission made by a person consists wholly or partly of material that is claimed by the person to be confidential or commercially sensitive; and  (b) the person has requested the body or association not to publish the material; and  (c) the body or association is satisfied that the material is confidential or commercially sensitive; then:  (d) if the submission consists wholly of the material—the body or association is not required to publish the submission on its website; or  (e) if:  (i) the submission consists partly of the material; and  (ii) it is practicable for the body or association to remove the material from the submission;  the body or association may remove the material from the submission before publishing the submission on its website; or  (f) if:  (i) the submission consists partly of the material; and  (ii) it is not practicable for the body or association to remove the material from the submission;  the body or association is not required to publish the submission on its website."@en ;
